Package: Triage
Type: Package
Title: Adjudication of Cell Type Annotations Using Biological Evidence and Cell Ontology Constraints
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Triage", family = "contributors", role = "aut",
        comment = "See git history for individual contributors"),
    person(given = "shaolab-UM", email = "linfanxiao.bio@gmail.com",
        role = "cre", comment = "Repository contact"))
Maintainer: shaolab-UM <linfanxiao.bio@gmail.com>
Description: Triage is a downstream workflow for adjudicating cell type
    annotations: candidate cell type annotations are generated upstream by
    separate annotation methods, and Triage evaluates those candidate
    annotations together with reviewer assignments, differential expression,
    enrichment evidence and Cell Ontology relationships to determine the
    supported cell identity and an appropriate level of specificity.
    CL-Linker maps free-text reviewer labels to Cell Ontology terms. The
    package provides deterministic postprocessing of Handling Editor
    adjudication outputs (normalization, release policy, consensus rules and
    the local validation gate); optional external LLM execution applies to
    the Handling Editor stage only. Chief QC and final release-state
    assignment are executed only by the batch pipeline scripts, not by the
    package API.
